tasks.prompt:
The function $f(x) = \dfrac{x}{x^2 + 4}$ is given for $x \in (-\infty;+\infty)$. Find:

a) the intervals of increase and decrease and the local extrema of the function;

b) the smallest and the largest value of the function on the interval $[-3;5]$;

c) the intervals of convexity and concavity and the inflection points of the function.
